Z||000000||baptistheart||07-11-2001||12:08 PM||||Does anyone know how to remove a front clip,the steps to be taken,how many bolts,what all needs to be disconnected?<BR>I did a search and came up with nothing but stuff for the rear clip.<BR>    thanks in advance!<P>------------------<BR>Joe||||reg||5
Z||000001||baptistheart||07-11-2001||03:08 PM||||bump<P>------------------<BR>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000002||286SE'S||07-11-2001||04:06 PM||||It is not difficult nor are there any secrets to getting it off. I found a nice SE front end at the junkyard once and decides it would  be a good idea to get it as a spare. I first removed the side marker lights and took out the screws under them. Then all the visible ones along the front trunk hinge area. Then I saw that the wheel well had screws going into the facia and removed those. Then lying on my back got under the front and took out a bunch on each side near the tires. It then just about fell off. Putting one one and aligning it would be more work! The turn signals are mounted on the space frame. Nothing to disconnect actually.||||reg||1
Z||000003||baptistheart||07-11-2001||07:02 PM||||Thanks I want to start this weekend but didn't know where to start, I did get the sunroof off however that was easier than expected too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Joe||||reg||1
